# The oldest jm-respproxy source commit the canonical compose may run.
# rollout-compose.sh --cutover-proxy / --proxy-restore read the proxy image's
# org.opencontainers.image.revision label and refuse unless this commit is an
# ancestor of it (git merge-base --is-ancestor) in the deploying checkout.
#
# e42737d: proxy-authored applied credential receipts, exact-byte reload
# validation, retained-session revocation before acknowledgment, and an
# exec entrypoint with one original process identity. The Manager requires
# this applied-reload protocol and never trusts signal-only acknowledgments.
# Inherits ce7483e stage-birth startup configuration, enforcing ownership
# prerequisites, and joined lease/proxy shutdown.
#
# Inherits 5fb0fab: the reload heartbeat. The
# Manager from the same change counts the proxy live only while
# reload.heartbeat is fresh, so an older image (no heartbeat) is refused
# every approval. It descends from a861a46 (whole-line reload ack) and from
# 733de16 (the merged H-8B lease engine: every-mode gate fa5d0fc,
# slice-accounting and counter hardening, per-project leases).
#
# The check is by ancestry, so this commit stays valid after a regular merge
# into the release line. A squash or rebase merge rewrites it: then set this
# file to the release-line commit that carries these proxy requirements.
#
# server/respproxy TestH8BGateCoversEntrypointHandshake enforces the bump
# for entrypoint.sh. It needs full git history: CI (.github/workflows/ci.yml)
# checks out with fetch-depth: 0 and sets JM_REQUIRE_GATE_HISTORY=1, so a
# shallow clone fails the test there instead of skipping it.
#
# Bump at each release that changes internal/respproxy OR
# server/respproxy/entrypoint.sh (its reload handshake is a contract with
# the Manager's principal store).
